      "text": "### 23CS201PE402\n\n### QUANTUM COMPUTING\n\n### L R P C\n\n2 0 2 3\n\nCourse type PROFESSIONAL\n\nELECTIVE Pre-requisite NA\n\nCourse Outcomes:\n\nAt the end of the course, the student will be able to:\n\nCO1: Apply quantum computing principles, quantum gates, and quantum circuits to develop basic\n\nquantum programs using Qiskit.\n\nCO2: Analyze quantum states, entanglement, noise, and quantum information concepts in quantum\n\ncomputing systems\n\nCO3: Implement and evaluate quantum algorithms such as Deutsch-Jozsa, Grover's Search, QFT,\n\nQPE, and Shor's Algorithm for computational problems\n\nCO4: Evaluate NISQ-era quantum hardware, error mitigation techniques, and hybrid quantum-\n\nclassical approaches for real-world applications\n\nCourse Articulation Matrix (CAM):",
