      "text": "circuit diagrams, simulation results, and compares quantum vs. classical complexity.\n\nProduct 3: Hybrid Quantum Optimization System\n\nObjectives: Develop a hybrid quantum-classical optimization application on a noisy quantum\n\nsimulator.\n\nKey Topics NISQ computing, parameterized circuits, VQE, QAOA, error mitigation, quantum\n\nhardware\n\nExpected Deliverable: A Qiskit application that solves a small optimization problem using\n\nVQE/QAOA, evaluates noisy vs. ideal execution, and reports performance metrics.\n\nText Books\n\n1. Bernhardt, C. “Quantum Computing for Everyone”. MIT Press, 2023.\n\n2. Hidary, J. “Quantum Computing an Applied Approach”. 2ndedn. Springer, 2022.\n\nReference Books\n\n1. Hundt, R. “Quantum Computing for Programmers”. O'Reilly Media,2022.\n\n2. Wong, H.Y.“Introduction to Quantum Computing From a Layperson to a Programmer”,\n\nSpringer, 2022.\n\nOnline Resources / Useful Links\n\n1. IBM Quantum Learning – Introduction to Quantum Computing and Qiskit\n\n(https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com)\n\n2. IBM Quantum Platform – Quantum Composer and Lab (https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/)\n\n3. Qiskit Documentation (https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides)\n\n4. Qiskit GitHub Repository (https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit)\n\n5. Google Quantum AI (https://quantumai.google/)\n\n6. Quantum Algorithm Zoo (https://quantumalgorithmzoo.org/)",
